{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1320395-can-t-make-sense-of-the-healing-example","id":1320395,"title":"Can't make sense of the Healing example","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-06-23T21:05:43-07:00","id":1320395,"title":"Can't make sense of the Healing example","content":"As noted, I'm having some trouble comprehending the example given on page 290.<br /> <br /> Now, as I read the rules, the PC in question would heal her physical 'Injured', 'Hurt' and 'Bruised' damage one at a time over the course of just three hours.<br /> <br /> Simultaneously, she's healing her 'Hurt' chimerical damage which finishes 9 hours after the physical damage is repaired and then begins healing the 'Bruised' level which takes 6 more hours.<br /> <br /> All in all, our heroine is all healed up in 18 hours. I get that this is close to the 'one day' described, but want to make sure I'm not missing something in the rules.<br /> <br /> TIA<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1666-firstborn8","name":"Firstborn8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-24T02:15:23-07:00","id":1320434,"title":"","content":"If your talking of the example where the heroine has suffered 2 lethal Chimerical damage and 3 bashing physical damage then yes there is a mistake in that example. Like said both health tracks heal simultaneusly which would mean that she would heal the first level of Chimerical Lethal in 12 hours while she already would have healed the first physical Bashing in one hour, the example mistakenly says it would take one day to heal that physical damage instead of one hour.<br /> <br /> That is to say your reading of the rules is correct but the example is flawed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-24T11:00:22-07:00","id":1320532,"title":"","content":"Yes, that was the one.<br /> <br /> The only other possible interpretation I could come up with was that the PC had to heal the 'Injured' first (1 hr), then healed the two 'Hurt' levels over the course of 12 hours, and finally healed the 'Bruised levels over the final 6 hours, but that still only added up to 19 hours total and seemed unnecessarily complicated to boot.<br /> <br /> Unfortunate as it is then, I'm glad the example was the problem...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1666-firstborn8","name":"Firstborn8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}